## Installation
If you’re intending to use the pre-compiled binaries, like {{model.binariesSentence}},
then installation on your system is a matter of copying the libraries, and 
binaries to your preferred install location, ensuring the libraries can be found 
at runtime, and the binaries are on your PATH.

If you’re intending to also use the C API, then you need to ensure the header 
files and also installed somewhere your build system can find them. We do not 
currently recommend using the C++ API with the pre-compiled `{{ model.libsaxonc }}` in
case of ABI conflict, for that you can compile `{{ model.libsaxonc }}` yourself.

If you’re intending to compile `{{ model.libsaxonc }}` yourself, then what you need to do
will depend on your project and its build system. We provide out-of-the-box 
compatibility with CMake, but using other systems should be straightforward.

### Installing the files
We recommend unpacking the release `.zip` under
`{{model.installPath}}`, and then adding the relevant
folders to your PATH and {{model.runtimeLinkerVar}} environment variables. This allows
you to install more than one version, or edition, side-by-side,
should you need it.

For example:

	mkdir -p {{model.installPrefix}}

    cd {{ model.installPrefix }}

    unzip /path/to/{{ model.releaseFileName }}


### Set the {{model.runtimeLinkerVar}} and PATH environment variables
The {{model.runtimeLinkerVar}} variable must be include the locations of the lib
directories containing the SaxonC libraries. For instance:

	export {{ model.runtimeLinkerVar }}="{{ model.SaxonCCorePackageLibPath }}:{{ model.SaxonCPackageLibPath }}:${{ model.runtimeLinkerVar }}"

If you’re only going to use the pre-compiled `{{ model.libsaxoncCore }}`, and compile
`{{ model.libsaxonc }}` yourself, you only need to add the `{{model.SaxonCCorePackage}}` lib path to
`{{ model.runtimeLinkerVar }}`.

To run the {{ model.editionBinariesSentence }} binaries without referencing their full
path, the PATH variable can be set. For instance:

	export PATH="{{ model.SaxonCPackageBinPath }}:$PATH"
